  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 453, the gross profit ratio equals gross profit divided by the contract price. Gross profit is $250,000 - $100,000 = $150,000. Contract price is $250,000. The ratio is $150,000 / $250,000 = 60%. Each payment is multiplied by 60% to determine recognized gain.
Wrong (A): 20% would result from dividing the down payment ($50,000) by the contract price, which is not how the gross profit ratio is calculated.
Wrong (B): 40% would apply if the basis were $150,000, but here the basis is $100,000, yielding a 60% ratio.
Wrong (D): 100% would mean zero basis, requiring the taxpayer to recognize every dollar received as gain.$EXPL$
