-- Q4352: Nontaxable Dispositions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1033, gain is recognized to the extent the amount realized exceeds the cost of replacement property. Gain realized is $150,000 ($400,000 - $250,000). Amount not reinvested is $50,000 ($400,000 - $350,000). Since $50,000 is less than the $150,000 realized gain, $50,000 is recognized.
Wrong (A): $0 would apply only if the entire $400,000 were reinvested. Here, $50,000 was not reinvested and must be recognized.
Wrong (C): $100,000 is the deferred gain amount, not the recognized gain. Recognition is limited to the amount not reinvested.
Wrong (D): $150,000 is the total realized gain, which would be recognized only if no replacement property were purchased.$EXPL$
