-- Q4353: Nontaxable Dispositions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 1033(b), the basis of replacement property equals its cost minus the deferred gain. Here, basis = $350,000 cost - $100,000 deferred gain = $250,000 + $50,000 recognized gain = $300,000. The deferred gain is embedded in the reduced basis for recognition upon eventual disposition.
Wrong (A): $350,000 is the cost of the replacement property before adjusting for deferred gain. The basis must be reduced by the $100,000 deferral.
Wrong (B): $400,000 is the insurance proceeds amount, which has no direct role in computing replacement property basis.
Wrong (C): $250,000 is the original property''s adjusted basis. The replacement property basis reflects cost minus deferred gain, yielding $300,000.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4353;

-- Q4355: Nontaxable Dispositions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 1033(g), when real property held for business or investment is condemned, the broader like-kind standard applies. The replacement need only be of like kind — the same nature or character — meaning any real property held for business or investment qualifies.
Wrong (A): Identical property is not required. Section 1033(g) applies the like-kind standard, which is broader than requiring the exact same property.
Wrong (B): Similar or related in service or use is the stricter standard for non-real-property conversions. Condemned real property uses the broader like-kind test.
